#NEXUS

[ turner2012a_fig1: Slanted cladogram of nine coelurosaur groups, read by eye; fully resolved. Dromaeosauridae's branch leaves the Troodontidae branch partway along, so the two are sisters and Avialae is their sister. The silhouettes are not encoded. 9 tips, fully resolved. Sample 6 case (census 2 extended to draw 120, seed 20261231). Topology transcribed from the figure image and checked node by node; topology only. ]

BEGIN TAXA;
    DIMENSIONS NTAX=9;
    TAXLABELS
        Tyrannosauridae
        Compsognathidae
        Ornithomimosauria
        Alvarezsauridae
        Therizinosauria
        Oviraptorosauria
        Troodontidae
        Dromaeosauridae
        Avialae
    ;
END;

BEGIN TREES;
    TREE turner2012a_fig1 = [&R] (Tyrannosauridae,(Compsognathidae,(Ornithomimosauria,(Alvarezsauridae,(Therizinosauria,(Oviraptorosauria,((Troodontidae,Dromaeosauridae),Avialae)))))));
END;
